      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "P.S. About the code\n\nIf you have to follow the ISO 639-3 code strictly, then we can use QTC as the code since \"qaa–qtz are 'reserved for local use' \".\n\nIf you don't have to follow the ISO code strictly, then we prefer keeping TEO as the code since it's easier to identify.\n\nSince Cantonese and Wu, these two Chinese dialects had been added recently, I wish Teochew could be added soon because our community at VRChat is growing larger and larger and already reach 160+ members. We also made our official website online.\n\nFeel free to comment if you have any questions, I will provide more infomations if needed.",
